{
  "schema": "airplanemode.runtime.benchmark/1",
  "id": "opfs-snapshot-readback",
  "title": "OPFS File snapshot taken the instant a write closes: size and checksum read back, 64 MiB and 600 MiB (Sprint 6)",
  "measuredAt": "2026-11-19",
  "commit": {
    "recorded": false,
    "base": "4f5b011",
    "note": "No commit hash was recorded. The runs were made on the Sprint 6 working tree on top of 4f5b011; that tree was committed on 2026-11-19 (0c002f4 to 7d3777b)."
  },
  "machine": {
    "label": "Apple M5 Pro 48 GB",
    "cores": 18,
    "os": "macOS arm64",
    "browser": "Google Chrome 157 (installed, Playwright channel \"chrome\"); the exact build is not recorded in this file"
  },
  "laptop8gb": "not measured on 8 GB",
  "method": "opfs-snapshot.spec.ts writes a synthetic file the way src/store/opfs.ts commits an asset (8 MiB chunk files, then createWritable), takes the File snapshot the instant close() resolves, posts it to a worker and reads it with arrayBuffer(), then compares the size and a 32-bit FNV-1a checksum with what was written. Variants: chunked 64 MiB x 50, one createWritable write 64 MiB x 20, chunked 64 MiB x 10 read 1.5 s later, and chunked 600 MiB x 3 read twice (the hash read, then the engine read). run1 is the console output of the run that docs/engine-load-retry.md quotes (the medians are in its summary lines); run2 is the JSON of a later run the same day with the per-iteration probes.",
  "commands": [
    "RUNTIME_MODEL=1 RUNTIME_MODEL_LEGS=wasm RUNTIME_SNAPSHOT_ITERATIONS=50 RUNTIME_MODEL_OUT=<dir> npx playwright test -c test/browser/playwright.model.config.ts opfs-snapshot"
  ],
