      "text": "[WebServer] \n[WebServer] (!) Some chunks are larger than 500 kB after minification. Consider:\n[WebServer] - Using dynamic import() to code-split the application\n[WebServer] - Use build.rollupOptions.output.manualChunks to improve chunking: https://rollupjs.org/configuration-options/#output-manualchunks\n[WebServer] - Adjust chunk size limit for this warning via build.chunkSizeWarningLimit.\n\nRunning 4 tests using 1 worker\n\nchunked-immediate {\"iterations\":50,\"snapshotSizeWrong\":0,\"readFailed\":0,\"readSizeWrong\":0,\"checksumWrong\":0,\"errors\":[],\"medianWriteMs\":116,\"medianReadMs\":35}\n  ✓  1 [chrome] › test/browser/opfs-snapshot.spec.ts:205:1 › D1-07: a 64 MiB file written through the store's chunked commit path and snapshotted immediately reads back whole, 50 times (8.0s)\nsingle-immediate {\"iterations\":20,\"snapshotSizeWrong\":0,\"readFailed\":0,\"readSizeWrong\":0,\"checksumWrong\":0,\"errors\":[],\"medianWriteMs\":58,\"medianReadMs\":34}\nchunked-held-1500ms {\"iterations\":10,\"snapshotSizeWrong\":0,\"readFailed\":0,\"readSizeWrong\":0,\"checksumWrong\":0,\"errors\":[],\"medianWriteMs\":112,\"medianReadMs\":35}\n  ✓  2 [chrome] › test/browser/opfs-snapshot.spec.ts:223:1 › D1-07: a single createWritable write snapshotted immediately, and a snapshot read 1.5 s after it was taken, read back whole (18.7s)\nchanged-after-snapshot {\"firstBefore\":1,\"after\":{\"ok\":false,\"name\":\"NotReadableError\"},\"probeAfter\":{\"ok\":false,\"name\":\"NotReadableError\"}}\n  ✓  3 [chrome] › test/browser/opfs-snapshot.spec.ts:243:1 › D1-07: a file changed after a snapshot was taken makes the OLD snapshot unreadable (NotReadableError), never a read of other bytes (R15, R20) (96ms)\nchunked-large-twice 600 MiB {\"iterations\":3,\"snapshotSizeWrong\":0,\"readFailed\":0,\"readSizeWrong\":0,\"checksumWrong\":0,\"errors\":[],\"medianWriteMs\":1441,\"medianReadMs\":837}\n  ✓  4 [chrome] › test/browser/opfs-snapshot.spec.ts:286:1 › D1-07: a model-sized file (600 MiB) written through the chunked commit path, snapshotted immediately and read twice (the hash read, then the engine read), reads back whole (7.2s)\n\n  4 passed (36.6s)\n"
